Interactive USD edits of lights of different types, with the usd procedural cache_id and with the render delegate

A sphere light lighting a grey wall gets spot shaping, whose cone angle changes, which is then removed, and is hidden
and shown again. It's replaced by a rect light, whose color is connected to a shader and that gets a light filter,
which are then removed. A dome light, a mesh light and a point instancer of spot lights are then added and edited.
The stage is re-rendered after each edit.
The scenario runs with the "usd" procedural reading the stage through its cache_id in an interactive render session,
and with the HdArnoldRendererPlugin render delegate driven like a Hydra host, see
testsuite/common/interactive_usd_test.h. Each render is checked in test.cpp, and the last procedural render is
compared against the reference image. Edits that aren't rendered correctly yet are reported as warnings (known issues
in test.cpp).

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {'program_env': 'interactive_usd'}
